","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2022-02-23T00:20:55Z","updated_at":"2022-08-21T03:37:14Z","closed_at":"2022-08-21T03:37:14Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Neovim version (nvim -v)\r\n\r\nv0.6.1\r\n\r\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\r\n\r\n~Not applicable; vim does not have lua~ Yes\r\n\r\n### Operating system/version\r\n\r\nArch Linux (5.16.9-arch1-1)\r\n\r\n### Terminal name/version\r\n\r\nMATE Terminal (1.26.0-1)\r\n\r\n### $TERM environment variable\r\n\r\nxterm-256color\r\n\r\n### Installation\r\n\r\n`pacman -S neovim`\r\n\r\n### How to reproduce the issue\r\n\r\n```vim\r\n:echo expand(\"~\")\r\n/home/xxx\r\n\r\n:let $HOME = \"1\"\r\n:echo expand(\"~\")\r\n1\r\n\r\n:call setenv(\"HOME\", \"2\")\r\n:echo expand(\"~\")\r\n1\r\n\r\n:lua vim.env.HOME = \"3\"\r\n:echo expand(\"~\")\r\n1\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nAll three assignments should have the same effect.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nOnly the `let $HOME` variant affects functions such as `expand`. (`echo $HOME` is affected however.)\r\n\r\n`let $HOME` is [special-cased](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/90a43e846d96255b35338e95b5841f913ce2c657/src/nvim/eval.c#L1867-L1875) to update a few internal cache variables, but the other methods [are not](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/726ec7fb17aa8a86b1c2c9adc4c6abfcb350d3a7/src/nvim/eval/funcs.c#L9277) (didn't find where the lua one is implemented).","closed_by":{"login":"zeertzjq","id":35768171,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzY4MTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35768171?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeertzjq","html_url":"https://github.com/zeertzjq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeertzjq/fo